content:
{
  "asset": "P-104 standby AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump on the filtered-water, sodium-hypochlorite-dosed line; serial plate unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal: the steady leakage matches the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal'. The documented corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement under procedure 5.2 and an alignment check under 5.4. No numerical allowable leakage rate is provided, so a numeric leak limit cannot be claimed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable manufacturer classification is Figure 3 for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings; the highest of the weekly readings from both housings must be classified. Taking the reported 3.0 mm/s at face value, it is within Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C (4.5–7.1, restricted/plan maintenance) and Zone D (7.1–11.0 as shown, damage likely/stop). Thus the reported value does not trigger the site rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature: the applicable HF-300 limits are for bearing-housing surface temperature: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. At 69 C, the reading is within the normal range, 1 C below the normal upper limit, 11 C below alarm and 21 C below trip. The site requirement for a priority-1 work order applies above the manufacturer's alarm limit and is not triggered at 69 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall decision: plan the required steady-leak repair as P2 corrective work. Neither the documented immediate-stop vibration condition nor the specific P1 overtemperature condition is met by the reported readings. This does not permit seal work while running; the pump must be isolated and drained for the repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces: assess first as the direct seal-failure mechanism listed for shaft-seal leakage; confirm during disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry: also listed as a probable cause. Check the Plan 11 flush arrangement and operating history because the manual requires discharge-derived seal flush and explicitly says never to run dry. No such history is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment: another documented cause of seal leakage. Check alignment rather than assuming it from the 3.0 mm/s reading, which remains in the long-term-operation zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Pre-work hold point: obtain a verified serial/build record before seal procurement or installation. Below serial HF3-22000, the manual/SB combination retains component seal HF3-450 and Table 5. At HF3-22000 and above, SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. If P-104's range cannot be established, keep both seal selection and gland torque on hold for technical disposition.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Make the pump safe before internal/seal work: electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves; drain and vent first and then complete the line-break permit. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-104 is within the chemically dosed P-101 to P-106 group.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare the lift: the back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the site's 25 kg threshold. Obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. Isolate and drain the pump, then remove the back pull-out assembly; the back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Inspect the removed seal for worn or cracked faces and investigate evidence of dry running or misalignment before finalising the cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For a verified bulletin-scope pump, replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth and fit pre-set HF3-450B; no sleeve measurement is needed to set that seal, but the separate scoring check still applies. For a verified pump below HF3-22000, fit HF3-450 under the manual procedure. In either case, fit the correct new seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten disturbed fasteners with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. For manual-scope HF3-450 installation, tighten M10 seal gland nuts to 25 Nm. For HF3-450B on a verified bulletin-scope pump, use the SB gland-nut torque of 30 Nm instead.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and achieve parallel offset of 0.05 mm and angular alignment of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before operation, ensure the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in service and never run the seal dry. After repair, record housing-surface temperature against the 70/80/90 C limits and measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings weekly, classifying the highest reading. If vibration falls in Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature exceeds the 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity one; replace whenever the casing is opened and fit a new gasket during mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component mechanical seal—conditional alternative only after verifying P-104 is below serial HF3-22000. Do not fit it on pumps at HF3-22000 or above. Do not treat this and HF3-450B as parts to install together.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal—conditional alternative only after verifying P-104 is at serial HF3-22000 or above; it replaces HF3-450 for that range and needs no sleeve measurement for seal setting.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve—conditional replacement for a verified SB-2026-014-scope pump when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Inspect the existing sleeve during disassembly; applicability on P-104 is unresolved until its serial range is known.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves: P-104 is on the filtered-water line within P-101 to P-106, which are dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out lift, use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment; the site threshold for these controls is any component heavier than 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current 3.0 mm/s reading is not in the highest severity zone. If subsequent classification is Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Pump-maintenance work: remove the back pull-out assembly and impeller, withdraw and inspect the seal and sleeve, fit the applicable seal and new casing gasket, and reassemble to the specified torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Alignment work: check the shaft alignment and provide laser-alignment capability after any work moving the motor or bearing housing; apply the 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular tolerances.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting supervision/support: the shift supervisor must sign the lifting plan, and certified lifting equipment is required for the 68 kg assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolation/permitting work: complete MCC LOTO, suction/discharge isolation, draining, venting and the line-break permit before starting seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reliability-engineer involvement is conditional, not presently triggered: notify the engineer before restart if vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland torque: the manual parts list and Table 5 specify HF3-450 and 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead requires HF3-450B at 30 Nm and prohibits HF3-450, but only for serial HF3-22000 and above; it explicitly retains HF3-450 and manual Table 5 below that serial. The bulletin therefore controls only within its stated scope, not universally. Because P-104's serial is unreadable, no evidence-based asset-specific selection can yet be made: hold the seal and torque decision pending serial verification rather than defaulting to either document.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve disposition: manual procedure 5.2 requires inspection for scoring but gives no numerical rejection limit. The SB's replace-when-scoring-exceeds-0.1-mm rule is stated for pumps in its serial scope. Apply that numerical rule to P-104 only after verifying it is HF3-22000 or above; the below-serial acceptance criterion remains undocumented.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is P-104's verified serial/build range? If it cannot be established, what seal and gland torque are technically authorised? The evidence supplies no fallback for an unreadable serial plate. [C05, C11, C13]",
    "Was the reported 3.0 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity reading on a bearing housing, and what were the readings on both bearing housings? The manual requires weekly measurement on both and classification of the highest reading, while only one value is reported. [C06, C07]",
    "Was the reported 69 C measured on the bearing-housing surface, the location to which the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits apply? [C01, C02]",
    "What are the seal-face condition, sleeve scoring depth, alignment result and Plan 11 flush/dry-running history? These inspections are needed to distinguish the listed causes and decide conditional sleeve replacement. [C02, C09, C10, C13]",
    "If P-104 is below HF3-22000, what sleeve-scoring acceptance or replacement criterion should be used? The manual only says to inspect for scoring; the 0.1 mm criterion is expressly in the serial-limited bulletin. [C10, C13]",
    "Is a numerical post-repair seal-leakage acceptance test required? The evidence gives the corrective action for leakage but no allowable leak-rate value. [C09]",
    "No labour-hour estimate, repair duration, required return-to-service date or general P2/P3 priority matrix is supplied; the site extract only documents specific P1 and emergency-stop triggers. P2 is therefore a planning judgement for the required leak repair, subject to site scheduling confirmation. [C09, C15]"
  ]
}
